{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1779717728,"nonce":"T+BPEhNYtw9JwBTggthm8GMnyyM=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDULhPc8AAAAGCX2RVA"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779735604,"nonce":"7hQwo8T5Hwq9PaIscTDYBL+cT/M=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDmYZog","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/170#issuecomment-4536539554"},"message":"## Offline validation: replay logged segmentation to find where this would trigger\n\nBefore field-testing, there's a ready-made offline test set. The forward-OAK **segmentation** the perception#17 adapter consumes is logged across most deployments in `~/data/logs/bizzy_images/` (`oak_forward/segmentation/compressed` + `camera_info` + `image_raw/ffmpeg`) — 2026-04-21 through 05-22.\n\nSuggested step: **replay the logged forward segmentation through the adapter + collision_monitor offline and catalog every point the node would trigger** (slow / stop), then cross-reference each trigger against the boat's track + speed (`/bizzy/odom` in the main deployment bags) and the per-host operator notes. That yields both real **true-positive** triggers (obstacles / moorings / shoreline) and **false positives** to tune the polygons against — across many deployments, no field time required. It also derisks the field test by showing how often it would have fired and on what.\n\nOn the 05-01 mooring-ball near-miss (#124 §7, ~14:21 EDT) that motivated this layer: heads-up that 05-01 imagery starts at **14:25 EDT — ~4 min after the near-miss** (`bizzy_images/bag_2026-05-01T14.25.43…`, covering ~14:25–16:29 EDT with a short gap), so the exact near-miss frame isn't in the logs. The surrounding ~2 h of forward segmentation is, and the other deployments add more material.\n\n**Polygon tuning for boat momentum** (your \"favor slowdown over hard stop, realistic standoff\"): from #124 §2 ([PR #172](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/172)), passive stopping is gentle — coast-down ≈0.15 m/s² (τ≈9–10 s) → **~10–15 m to stop from cruise (~1.5 m/s)**. So the slow/standoff zone must extend well beyond ~15 m at cruise, or the monitor needs to command reverse rather than just zero throttle. Active crash-stop braking distance is uncharacterized — folded into #88.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779803595,"nonce":"66bKif8fIUsoVUcroCQp2W9KGmU=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDULhPc8AAAAGC-stpA"},"status":2}]}